   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to authorize Peter G. LaSala to elect to participate in the optional twenty-year retirement plan for police officers employed by the village of Potsdam in the county of St. Lawrence",
    "basePrintNo": "S5043",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5043-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Retirement",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5043\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to authorize Peter G. LaSala to elect to participate in the\noptional twenty-year retirement plan for police officers employed by\nthe village of Potsdam in the county of St. Lawrence\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nTo grant the Village of Potsdam Police Officer, Peter G. LaSala,\ntwenty-year retirement authorization.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection one allows Peter G. LaSala to be entitled to the full rights\nand benefits associated with coverage of the twenty-year retirement by\nfiling a request with the state comptroller on or before December 31,\n2017.\n\nSection two says the Village of Potsdam, within the next ten years,\nwill pay any past service costs incurred by the implementation of this\nbill.\n\nSection three is the effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nFor reasons not ascribable to his own negligence, Peter G. LaSala,\nfailed to make a timely application to participate in such optional\ntwenty-year retirement system. The Village of Potsdam Board of\nTrustees has requested this legislation.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\n2016 - S. 7694 Passed Senate/A. 10181 - Government Employees Committee\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone to the State.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
